<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue name="Imperium - Adeptus Astartes" id="9e71-33d7-c8a4-d662" authorContact="Centuria Astartes Discord, ask for AHeras." authorName="A. Heras" authorUrl="Centuria Astartes Discord" battleScribeVersion="2.03" gameSystemId="5b78-3a13-0882-b019" gameSystemRevision="4" library="false" revision="1" type="catalogue" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema">
  <comment>General cost tool:
20pts=1pl
Marine-20pts &gt;&gt; 2Marine-25pts
Jetpack &gt;&gt; Collective-&gt;5pts Singular-&gt;10pts
Bike &gt;&gt; 10pts
Terminator Armour &gt;&gt; 25pts
Veteran &gt;&gt; 5pts
Relic Equipment &gt;&gt; Collective-&gt;10pts Singular-&gt;15pts</comment>
  <readme>Inspired from the original Warhammer 40,000 9th Edition database, created by BSData Developers, @WH40k Data Dev, from https://www.bsdata.net/contact.

Additional reference data obtained from Wahapedia, https://wahapedia.ru/

Well...it&apos;s a test, read carefuly the rules, as a lot of them are changed or even re-writed from the ground up.
It&apos;s possible to found some mistakes, this database is complex, as it condenses all the Astartes chapters in one system.
Sorry if someone lose the hope due to the invulnerable saves drain, or general point escalation, but that&apos;s the point of this experiment anyways.

Have fun!

A.</readme>
